  <!--
    CHARMM36 / AMBER ff14SB + OL3 parameters for RNA 8-oxoguanosine (8OG)
    =========================================================================
    Residue name:  8OG  (PDB convention for 8-oxoguanosine in RNA)
    Variants:      8OG (internal), 8OG5 (5'-terminal), 8OG3 (3'-terminal)

    Load this file TOGETHER with amber14/RNA.OL3.xml and amber14/tip3p.xml.

    Charge source: Derived by analogy from Aduri et al., J. Chem. Theory
      Comput. 2007, 3, 1464-1475 (AMBER modified RNA nucleoside parameters).
      Backbone/sugar charges are identical to guanosine (G) in RNA.OL3.xml.
      Base atoms near the 8-oxo modification (C8, O8, N7, H7) are estimated
      from RESP charge redistribution principles; the remaining base atoms
      retain exact G values.

    Net residue charge: -1.0 (phosphate form, same as G).

    Atomic changes vs. G:
      Removed:  H8  (aromatic CH on C8 in guanine)
      Changed:  C8  RNA-CP → RNA-C   (sp2 aromatic → sp2 carbonyl C)
                N7  RNA-NB → RNA-NA  (aromatic N → sp2 N-H)
      Added:    O8  RNA-O             (C8=O8 carbonyl oxygen)
                H7  RNA-H             (N7-H proton)

    VALIDATION: Run scripts/validate_8OG_ff.py before production use.
    RECOMMENDATION: Replace approximate charges with QM RESP values
      (antechamber on Linux server) once the pipeline is established.
